# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

CampusShare is a resource-sharing platform designed for colleges, universities, laboratories, makerspaces, research facilities, community organisations and small businesses.

Institutions frequently own equipment and spaces that remain unused for long periods. At the same time, students, researchers and project teams may lack access to these resources because purchasing or privately renting them is expensive.

CampusShare solves this problem by allowing authorised people to list, discover, reserve, use and return shared resources through a trusted digital platform.

The platform must support:

- Laboratory management.
- Equipment inventory management.
- Classroom and meeting-room reservations.
- Resource availability calendars.
- Student booking requests.
- Instructor approval workflows.
- Eligibility and safety verification.
- Fair allocation of limited resources.
- Check-in and check-out.
- Before-and-after condition reports.
- Damage and delay reporting.
- Maintenance scheduling.
- Notifications.
- Audit history.
- Resource utilisation analytics.
- Institution-level administration.

The primary demonstration use case should be an engineering college, with an Electronics and Communication Engineering department and its laboratories.

The application must also support other departments and institutions through configurable resource categories and institutional settings.

